Maintainer: Hyper-jiawei <https://github.com/Hyper-jiawei>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), dbus, systemd, polkitd, network-manager, iproute2, iputils-ping, mount, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 46)
Provides: owly
Conflicts: owly
Replaces: owly
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyper-jiawei/owly-airdrop-ubuntu
Description: AirDrop between iPhone and Ubuntu, with component-based desktop UI
 Owly (t4t5/owly) lets Linux use Apple's AirDrop protocol. This package
 bundles the original owly 0.4.2 radio daemon and CLI together with a
 component-based Ubuntu desktop integration:
  - GTK3 graphical app for receiving (auto-accept) and sending files
  - GNOME Shell quick-settings toggle with live readiness status
  - Headless controller (owly-ctl) for the toggle
  - Custom AirDrop icons, desktop launcher, Chinese documentation
 .
 The original owly source code is included in the source repository for
 secondary development. Licensed under MIT (T4T5 and contributors).
